.TH "cbor::limits" 3 "Version 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
cbor::limits \- Gives the limits of the build\&.  

.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.PP
\fR#include <cbor/validity\&.hpp>\fP
.SS "Static Public Attributes"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "static constexpr std::size_t \fBstring_length\fP = CBOR_STRING_LENGTH_DEFAULT"
.br
.RI "The bytes of one text or byte string; more give \fRstring_length_exceeded\fP\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "static constexpr std::size_t \fBcontainer_elements\fP = CBOR_CONTAINER_ELEMENTS_DEFAULT"
.br
.RI "The elements of an array, or the pairs of a map; more give \fRcontainer_elements_exceeded\fP\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "static constexpr std::size_t \fBamplification_activation_threshold\fP = CBOR_AMPLIFICATION_ACTIVATION_THRESHOLD_DEFAULT"
.br
.RI "The bytes that \fBcbor::encode()\fP of a tree writes before \fR\fBmaximum_amplification\fP\fP applies\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "static constexpr std::size_t \fBmaximum_amplification\fP = CBOR_MAXIMUM_AMPLIFICATION_DEFAULT"
.br
.RI "The most bytes that \fBcbor::encode()\fP writes for each byte of the tree; more give \fRamplification_limit_breach\fP\&. "
.in -1c
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
Gives the limits of the build\&. 

The macro \fRCBOR_STRING_LENGTH_DEFAULT\fP sets \fR\fBstring_length\fP\fP, and the macro \fRCBOR_CONTAINER_ELEMENTS_DEFAULT\fP sets \fR\fBcontainer_elements\fP\fP\&. A macro that the build does not set gets its default, \fRSIZE_MAX\fP\&. No call reads a limit at run time\&. A limit at \fRSIZE_MAX\fP is not set, and its check is not in the program\&. A limit counts what a call reads or decodes\&. An item that a call only skips does not count\&. Every translation unit of one program uses the same values\&.

.PP
Nesting has no fixed limit\&. A reader that recurses stops where the stack of its thread ends: a call that comes within 16 KiB of the end (32 KiB on Windows or with a sanitizer) returns \fRnesting_depth_exceeded\fP\&. Each thread reads the bounds of its own stack once, at its first check: from the system on Linux (glibc and musl), macOS and Windows, and from the linker on WebAssembly without threads and on picolibc\&. Another target does not compile\&. A frame outside these bounds, such as the stack of a fiber or of a signal handler, is not checked\&. The first check of a thread does not run in a signal handler\&. On Linux, a change of \fRRLIMIT_STACK\fP after the first check, and a mapping that a program places with \fRMAP_FIXED\fP below the stack of the main thread, are outside the bound\&. On picolibc, a stack smaller than the reserve refuses every nested item\&. \fBcbor::item_size()\fP, \fBcbor::sequence_reader\fP and a path of child segments do not recurse and read any depth\&. A deep value of a user type (\fR\fBstructs\fP\fP, \fR\fBstructs as Packed CBOR, with fields at fixed offsets\fP\fP) is destroyed and copied by its own recursion: a thread with a smaller stack than the one that decoded it can overflow there\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
cbor::limits::string_length      → std::size_t
cbor::limits::container_elements → std::size_t
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
.nf
message: {}
call: cbor::limits::string_length
result: 4294967295
call: cbor::limits::container_elements
result: 4294967295

.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
    // a build that sets no macro
    std::size_t const strings = cbor::limits::string_length;          // SIZE_MAX
    std::size_t const containers = cbor::limits::container_elements;  // SIZE_MAX
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBcbor::error\fP 
.RE
.PP

